\section{Why two files}{

The README and the front page differ in exactly two ways: pkgdown turns ANSI
SGR escapes into HTML while GitHub shows the raw bytes, so \code{index.md} keeps
colour and \code{README.md} has it stripped; and everything from the first
horizontal rule onwards belongs on GitHub, while pkgdown puts that material
in its sidebar.

\code{index.md} is written only when it would differ from \code{README.md}, and
\code{.Rbuildignore} is kept in step either way.
}

\section{Package-specific touch-ups}{

A README may define \code{readme_only()} or \code{index_only()} in a chunk, each
taking and returning a character vector. Each is applied to just that one
output.
